{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384936-10-conventions-instead-of-5","id":1384936,"title":"10 conventions instead of 5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-30T15:18:13-07:00","id":1384936,"title":"10 conventions instead of 5?","content":"Reading the preview of the Kickstarter got me thinking about one thing: Why does the technocracy have 5 conventions when there are 9 spheres (or ten if you count the &quot;ultimate&quot; sphere)? and just for curiosity, what new conventions would you create to fill the missing seats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:45:53-07:00","id":1384943,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't necessarily try to structure them according to the Spheres. That said, TR does make a couple of suggestions such as splitting the NWO up into an espionage-oriented Convention (Panopticon) and a bureaucracy-oriented Convention (the White Tower); and these do correlate fairly well with Data for Panopticon and Mind for the White Tower. There's also a suggestion of splitting off the study of Matter from the Progenitors and expanding it from just pharmaceuticals to all things chemistry-related. I'm not sure any of that is warranted; but that's not really the point of this thread, right? <br /> <br /> So at this point, we would have seven Conventions: Panopticon for Data, Void Engineers for Dimensional Science, Iteration X for Forces, the Progenitors for Life, a new Convention for Matter, the Ivory Tower for Mind, and the Syndicate for Primal Utility. <br /> <br /> That would leave only Entropy and Time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T19:24:30-07:00","id":1384985,"title":"","content":"The Convention of Matter could take a bit from ItX since they deal with material sciences as well to give them a bit more going for them than just splitting up the Progenitors.<br /> <br /> I personally think an interesting faction that could be a mix of NWO and Syndicate operatives would be a QA and destruct test division that focuses on Entropy. They're the ones that take what the researcher build, and then decided what makes it to the higher ups for inclusion in different programs (or not), and have their own separate organization to avoid bias.<br /> <br /> Time is harder because the biggest users of Time are probably going to be the higher ups of the Union that are working on projections and the Time Table, rather than a specific Convention that specializes in temporal mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T19:47:31-07:00","id":1384988,"title":"","content":"Iteration X also has the Time Motion Managers; if that's not a entropy thing I don't know what is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T21:21:53-07:00","id":1384999,"title":"","content":"Despite the name, the TM Managers aren't really about Entropy (even if most would pick some up just like they'd pick up Prime). ItXer's Statisticians are the Conventions Entropy heavy faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T23:21:35-07:00","id":1385015,"title":"","content":"As for the why? The Technocracy didn't form it's conventions in Terms of the spheres. Mostly, they are the current form of their historical counterparts... Somewhat. <br /> <br /> Though if I wanted to I would give Iteration X matter, NWO mind, Progenitors Life, the Syndicate Prime, the Void Engineers Spirit, and just make new groups for correspondence, entropy, forces, and time.<br /> <br /> Edit: maybe some sort of virtual adept counterpart for Correspondence, statistician group for entropy, power generation and distribution type group for Forces, and history rewriting group for time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 05-01-2020, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T18:35:28-07:00","id":1385164,"title":"","content":"It seems like there hasn't been enough time since the Virtual Adepts defection for another whole convention specializing in Correspondence to arise. I suppose I can see Iteration X having branched out to cover both Forces and Matter since the Electrodyne Engineers broke with the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T18:47:28-07:00","id":1385167,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that the Data Sphere variant of Correspondence was introduced in the NWO Convention Book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T19:35:29-07:00","id":1385175,"title":"","content":"One thing to remember about the Technocracy not being built around the spheres is that they predate them. The Order of Reason predates the Council of Traditions by more than 100 years. It was the Traditions that codified the Spheres into the 9 spheres we have today. <br /> <br /> The Technocracy doesn't think along the line of Science (Magick) being divided into the classification of spheres, so why would they adopt their conventions around them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T22:27:56-07:00","id":1385194,"title":"","content":"At the same time, The Order of Reason drew their membership from mages from the same groups that were instrumental in promoting the Nine Sphere model of magic among the Traditions; being significantly influenced by the kabbalistic Hermetics and Singers.<br /> <br /> The Union does sort of have to include the Spheres in how they construct their views on their &quot;science&quot; because it's still how they do it. Their beliefs let them operate under variant Spheres, but not to the point of completely reworking the Spheres to match a more modern breakdown of universal disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T08:46:36-07:00","id":1385246,"title":"","content":"Also, for game purposes, it's a lot easier to use that Spheres model for all characters. If you have a variant sphere such as Data or Dimensional Sciences to replace Correspondence or Spirit, respectively, it's a lot easier to play the game than if you had separate powers for each faction in a nonlinear magic system. In the end, gameplay also influences the spheres.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, they could have just stuck with noun-verb like Ars Magica and other games that do noun-verb magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T09:55:49-07:00","id":1385260,"title":"","content":"It's not that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy\">an alternative to the Spheres</a> couldn't be done; it just takes a lot of work. And it's not particularly conducive to mixed Mage/Technocracy games (though it doesn't actually render them impossible).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T10:43:59-07:00","id":1385267,"title":"","content":"Well indeed the preview hint to a possible Reorg based on the &quot;10 spheres of influence&quot; of the technocracy that will be more detailled in the last section of the book. The exemples given right now are a possible division of the NWO between Panopticon (Data?) and the Ivory tower (Mind), and the division of life based Progenitors and Matter based ones.<br /> <br /> Following such pattern, I would bet on ItX divided between Weapon crafting/Strike force cyborgs/Engineers (Forces) and Time management (Time), The Syndicate between &quot;Money and primal energy generation&quot; (Primal utility) and control of society (Entropy) and the Void Engineer between Pandimentional exploration and defense (dimensional science) and &quot;every other places to explore (Correspondance).<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm assuming that the &quot;10 spheres of influence&quot; are the 9 sphere wil Primal utility as Prime + the Data sphere. It may well be 9 spheres including Data as Correspondance + Primal utility. In which case I would rather divide the Void engineers between explorers (Dimensional science), and Constructs creation and maintainance (Prime).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T21:34:17-07:00","id":1385997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384936-10-conventions-instead-of-5?p=1385175#post1385175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to remember about the Technocracy not being built around the spheres is that they predate them. The Order of Reason predates the Council of Traditions by more than 100 years. It was the Traditions that codified the Spheres into the 9 spheres we have today.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy doesn't think along the line of Science (Magick) being divided into the classification of spheres, so why would they adopt their conventions around them?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were using the Spheres system in the Renaissance according to Sorcerer's Crusade. And the Council predates the Union by a few hundred years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T21:45:55-07:00","id":1385998,"title":"","content":"Err\u2026 you're right about the Sorcerers Crusade having everyone (Traditions <i>and</i> Order of Reason, and Disparates too) using the same nine Spheres. But the Order of Reason was the older group, having been around for at least a century before the Traditions organized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T23:00:38-07:00","id":1386013,"title":"","content":"True, but the Order of Hermes predates them by a few hundred years. And two game companies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T23:24:12-07:00","id":1386015,"title":"","content":"The Order of Hermes certainly predated the Order of Reason. But the <i>Spheres</i> didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T03:46:41-07:00","id":1386035,"title":"","content":"The concept of the spheres was actually developed by predecessors of the Order Of Reason - and of Hermes. At least if you believe the Unreliable Narrators.<br /> According to them, it was actually the cult of Thothmes in ancient egypt that formed the principles of the 'Nine Cornerstones' - which is now called the spheres.<br /> <br /> Both the Order Of Hermes and the Order Of Reason/Union (Given that parts of them are kind of a Hermes offshoot..) kind of see Thothmes as a common predecessor for some things - heck, the Technocracy has an incredible interest in the lost scrolls of Thothmes according to GttT and NWO Revised - which is why the Order Of Reason/Union, just like the Traditions (through Hermes), uses those 9 spheres of influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-06-2020, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T05:11:09-07:00","id":1386044,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll have to check my canon-lore-fu, but I thought the Spheres were categorized by the Order of Hermes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T06:23:27-07:00","id":1386051,"title":"","content":"I'll mess things up even more. No books with me atm, and I'm not sure if its Sorcerers Crusade or Mage books, but I thought the spheres weren't categorized until the founding of the Council of Traditions. I remember somewhere it being said the Hermetics even proposed something like 300 schools of Magick. Probably because every one of them wanted a seat on the council.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T08:27:26-07:00","id":1386087,"title":"","content":"The CoT starts up in the early 14th century (I think), during a meeting at the ruins of Mistridge.On a side note, we destroyed Mistridge in Ars Magia also (I helped write that book). But we kept the story simpler. Just one guy with a grude and some allies. Said allies were eventually absorbed into House Ex-Miscellanea as the Rusticani (Craftmasons).<br /> Back to Spheres.<br /> I kinda remember back in 1st edition, the concept was that there were always Spheres. I think. I have not followed this game closely until recently. I dropped off after 2nd ed and was a pure Ars Magica junkie for years. Still am. I started back into Mage last year with Sorcerers Crusade, then jumped to M20. So there is a lot of inbetween stuff I have not red. I am collecting it currently, but it is a lot to take in. And I am gonna skip Dark Ages (if I want a middle ages game, I would rather play Ars Magica. I enjoy Mage because it is a modern setting).<br /> <br /> Now, for the subject of Conventions, not basing it on magic styles at all, I do like the idea of a two (or even three) way split in some groups. I like the ideas I have seen mentioned about a Technocratic Schism of sorts. NWO, besides being a very dated name, is based on old fashioned concepts of globalism. I can see a split in methodology based on the same ideals. So a second organization within the NWO, such as The White Tower or Friends of John Courage, would be quite fitting. Same down the line for each convention.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:33:18-07:00","id":1386113,"title":"","content":"The problem with skipping Dark Ages Mage, is that it's a canon book for MtA, and it demonstrates that the early mages didn't use the Sphere system.<br /> <br /> By Sorcerer's Crusade, everybody (even uninvolved Crafts) are using Spheres.<br /> <br /> The only way to square that is to accept that the unification of mages caused by events between these two eras resulted in a modification or reality itself. Just like the Order of Reason's efforts changed things so that Sleeper belief had a more drastic impact on local Reality Zones, the Hermetics and the Craftmasons, with their shared backgrounds in magical theory, ended up pushing everyone into a world where Spheres is how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T11:13:40-07:00","id":1386128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384936-10-conventions-instead-of-5?p=1386113#post1386113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with skipping Dark Ages Mage, is that it's a canon book for MtA, and it demonstrates that the early mages didn't use the Sphere system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they used a system of 5 Techniques and 10 Forms LoL<br /> <br /> I am not so much concerned with &quot;cannon&quot;. I can adjust it to my whims for my purposes, and some answers may not exist. Which not to say I totally disregard cannon. It serves as a common base from which we can comprehend permutations and adjustments to the setting.<br /> As for Dark Ages Mage, I thought that was part of Vampire cannon, as it was not its own game. Or maybe not. But anyways, I don't feel obligated to consider it &quot;cannon&quot;, just as Ars Magica history is not (and cannot) be cannon.<br /> <br /> I just remembered something. There are countless &quot;Minor&quot; Spheres, correct? The core M20 includes a few technocrat spheres. I seem to remember in some olld book some rules for designing and using an alternate Sphere.I can imagne a faction from a convention focused on that. Something like a sphere that focuses on Quantum Physics, aspects of Forces and Matter, yet only a sliver from each, combined into one Sphere. (That was just a brainstorm idea with flaws, but you can see where I am going).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T11:23:37-07:00","id":1386131,"title":"","content":"The Traditions were formed in 1466, in reaction to the founding of the Order of Reason in 1325. This, in turn, was over a century after the destruction of Mistridge (1210) and the Dark Ages timeframe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T12:35:27-07:00","id":1386145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384936-10-conventions-instead-of-5?p=1386128#post1386128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can adjust it to my whims for my purposes, and some answers may not exist. Which not to say I totally disregard cannon. It serves as a common base from which we can comprehend permutations and adjustments to the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why Dark Ages Mage has to matter to this. It serves as part of that common base.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Dark Ages Mage, I thought that was part of Vampire cannon, as it was not its own game. Or maybe not. </div> </div> </div>The Revised Dark Ages books initially required Dark Ages Vampire for the core rules (though WW quickly reversed that an published the core rules sans VtM stuff as a free document so people could play the other DA gamelines without needing to worry about vampires) but were fully integrated into their modern gamelines narratively; unlike the earlier Vampire: the Dark Ages 2e supplements (of which only Werewolf got a full book) which was much more vampire-centric.<br /> <br /> There are Revised Mage books that had rotes with both the modern Spheres and DA era Pillars listed for them.<br /> <br /> DA Mage is most certainly its own game that's part of the Ascension game line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But anyways, I don't feel obligated to consider it &quot;cannon&quot;, just as Ars Magica history is not (and cannot) be cannon. </div> </div> </div>Canon. And you don't really get to say if a book is or isn't canon. It's the IP owners that decided that. You get to decided if you care.<br /> <br /> DA Mage is canon to Ascension because the owners of Mage say it is. AM isn't canon to Ascension because the owners say it isn't.<br /> <br /> If you have a compelling reason to ignore DA Mage, by all means present it. Otherwise is seems very iffy to just toss it out because you don't use it. It's an exceedingly relevant book to the topic of whether or not the Technocracy should be bound by the Sphere system, as it presents a time in Mage's history when mages weren't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are countless &quot;Minor&quot; Spheres, correct? </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. Minor Spheres were an optional rule from older editions that let mages excel in a specific aspect of a Sphere. If the optional rule is in play, then yes there are countless of them due to how broad the Spheres are and how many different ways you can chop them up into smaller pieces.<br /> <br /> Variant Spheres, which M20 does include are reskins of the base Spheres with a few tweaks to them. Data is not a Minor Sphere of Correspondence. It's variation on Correspondence that does things a bit differently, but still mostly does the same things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 05-06-2020, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:21:53-07:00","id":1386164,"title":"","content":"\u201cMinor Spheres\u201d was something introduced in the MRev Storyteller's Handbook. They were never \u201ccanon\u201d. The three Technocratic Sphere variants took three Spheres that are problematic for the Technocratic worldview (Correspondence, Prime, and Spirit) and reworked them into something more in sync with Enlightened Science: Dimensional Science was originally introduced as a way to address the fact that the Gauntlet is stronger in civilized areas and weaker out in the wilderness, which meant that the <i>worst</i> place for the Void Engineers to try to use it to cross over into the Umbra would be at a Technocratic stronghold. The original version of Dimensional Science was basically Spirit with a slight tweak to allow VE bases to be reasonable launch points for expeditions into the Umbra. And for over 20 years, that's how things stood: other than the Foundation and Pillars system from Dark Ages: Mage, nearly everything Mage-related used the nine Spheres as written, with the VE's Dimensional Science being the sole and extremely minor exception. <br /> <br /> (Incidentally, Dark Ages: Mage is technically a Dark Ages: Vampire supplement in that you needed to own the latter to have the full set of rules to play the game; but I say \u201ctechnically\u201d because the book wasn't written the way you'd expect a supplement to be written: it wasn't written in terms of \u201chere are some guys to serve as allies and/or antagonists for your vampire protagonists\u201d; it was written with mages being the protagonists in their own right, and any mention of vampires in the book was largely incidental.)<br /> <br /> It wasn't until the Revised Convention Books came out in 2012 that the Technocratic Sphere variants really became a thing: the NWO Convention Book introduced Data, which was conceived as a variant of Correspondence that was introduced to replace the more mystical Correspondence Range table with something more suited for Enlightened Science; the Syndicate book introduced a variant of Prime (\u201cPrimal Utility\u201d) that replaced earlier attempts to talk about Prime as a kind of energy field with something that aligns better with the economic theories of the Syndicate. And the VE book expanded on Dimensional Science's differences from Spirit and introduced a different variant of Correspondence that made distance a bigger part of it \u2014 though that variant just replaced the Correspondence Range table with another one, making it a \u201cvariant Sphere\u201d to about the same extent that the original Dimensional Science was a variant Sphere. And then M20 went and promoted the Sphere variants from Convention-specific things to \u201cthis is how the Technocracy sees the Spheres\u201d. <br /> <br /> There's room in M20 for some revisionism as to the Technocratic Spheres; but I'd still want the result to resemble, if not entirely parallel, the breakdown used by the Traditions. But that's a topic for another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:40:38-07:00","id":1386167,"title":"","content":"Jees Heinig wrote up the minor Sphere\u2019s in the MRev Storyteller\u2019s Handbook after suggestions made to do so from a few of us (I was there!) on the old White Wolf forums. What this illustrates is that anything can be \u2018canon\u2019 in your own games, including, your own Sphere categories. There isn\u2019t any reason you can\u2019t redesign them now, for your own games. If a game developer decided to change them in a new edition or whatever, (s)he would have to justify it, but it could be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T14:15:29-07:00","id":1386175,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Please understand that I love debate and I am not starting a fight.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384936-10-conventions-instead-of-5?p=1386145#post1386145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> Canon. And you don't really get to say if a book is or isn't canon. It's the IP owners that decided that. You get to decided if you care.<br /> <br /> DA Mage is canon to Ascension because the owners of Mage say it is. AM isn't canon to Ascension because the owners say it isn't.<br /> <br /> If you have a compelling reason to ignore DA Mage, by all means present it. Otherwise is seems very iffy to just toss it out because you don't use it. It's an exceedingly relevant book to the topic of whether or not the Technocracy should be bound by the Sphere system, as it presents a time in Mage's history when mages weren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>But anyways, I would point to Trippy's comment, that &quot;...anything can be \u2018canon\u2019 in your own games&quot;. So yeah, I get to decide if I care, but I also get to determine how it is handled in a game I run, and I am also free to influence people and advocate for dropping aspects of cannon. Not that I am doing so. I am just laying out a position that &quot;cannon&quot; is not that important.<br /> As for a &quot;compelling reason&quot;, for myself I need nothing more than the fact that I am just not into DA Mage, I would rather retcon the history of Ars Magica into a campaign (the two games were linked at one time).<br /> As for a compelling reason for *you*, I have none. If it is what you like and want to do, then by all means. However, as a discussion point as to why (this or that), it is but a minor point. But it *is* a valid point to make, and can help shed light on some ideas. But at the same time, it does not serve as a closing argument.<br /> <br /> I would also add that, with each new edition of a game, the &quot;cannon&quot; of previous editions becomes optional or is to be ignored. M20 makes mention of the Technocratic variant Spheres. So these are now part of M20 cannon. But none of the M20 books ever mention this alternate magic system from DA Mage. So, I would make the argument that these mechanical systems are no longer cannon. In fact, say one were to write a SV source-book or adventure set in the DA Mage era. I would feel that the author would be entirely justified in just using Spheres and the systems from M20. Ignore the pillars. Save space for details of the story and other goodies. I do not feel it is cool to require someone to track down and buy an old book that is otherwise imcompatible with the 600 page book that the adventure/sourcebook is based on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T14:33:12-07:00","id":1386178,"title":"","content":"As Heavy Arms said, some of the revised Tradition Books referred to the Foundation and Pillars system found in DA:Mage. In particular, the Verbena book listed Old Faith Seasons required to perform the Effects presented in that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T14:46:49-07:00","id":1386181,"title":"","content":"Point taken. But then again, those are books from a previous edition published over fifteen years ago. They are also books I do not (yet) have). What I *do* have is the entire M20 line, which should be more than enough. I also have the entire SC lline (except for one book on PDF only). Having said that, I *am* working on collecting these books. Spending my stimulus on e-bay <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It is not that I feel I need them to run a game. I just wanna read them and pluck ideas out of them. But I do feel that is enough of an investment, and I am not in the mood to chase down and buy up another line of mage books. I have not even finished my Ars Magica collection for the current edition. And I am curious about 5th ed D&amp;D. My attention span can only stretch so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T17:38:42-07:00","id":1386216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384936-10-conventions-instead-of-5?p=1386175#post1386175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />I am just laying out a position that &quot;cannon&quot; is not that important.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as you said yourself, canon is important to providing the base for discussions.<br /> <br /> For discussion the evolution of the Spheres system in-universe, the canon fact that in the past mages were not bound to the Sphere system is an important canon fact towards framing the rest of the conversation.<br /> <br /> However you or anyone else plays the game with this information in hand doesn't change the base state of how the setting is (messily) defined.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for a compelling reason for *you*, I have none. If it is what you like and want to do, then by all means. </div> </div> </div>To be clear about two things:<br /> <br /> 1) I mean a compelling reason for the discussion.<br /> <br /> 2) I will never run DA Mage because, while there's a lot of good in it, the Pillars mechanics are, for me, one of the worst design choices in the entire history of Mage. But that doesn't change that the book exists, and its content is relevant, and thus needs examination to the larger discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But at the same time, it does not serve as a closing argument. </div> </div> </div>It hasn't been used as such. My initial &quot;closing argument,&quot; was that reconciling DA Mage and Sorcerer's Crusade requires an acknowledgement that magic was changed fundamentally by the events of that time period (which happened in other aspects of magic as well).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would also add that, with each new edition of a game, the &quot;cannon&quot; of previous editions becomes optional or is to be ignored. </div> </div> </div>That's not how canon works.<br /> <br /> Canon, remembering its theological source in meaning, doesn't require works to even be consistent with each other, let alone things like changes between editions in a RPG. The 1e Mage books are still canon, because they're still official Mage books; even if many elements in them have been superseded by later books. RPG conventions around canon generally state that changes made in new editions take precedence over older material; even if the older material is still canon.<br /> <br /> The Star Wars franchise had a different heuristic for reconciling contradictions between canon sources based on that kind of medium the information comes from (the movies trump everything else, etc.) rather than order of release. So a novel written in in the 90s that's an official SW novel that contradicts something from A New Hope is superseded by the original film. Though that was simplified and revised once Disney took over with tighter control over media secondary to the films to ensure greater cohesion and continuity.<br /> <br /> Canon, ultimately, just means, &quot;the stuff that the ruling authority on the body of works considers officially part of the body of work.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But none of the M20 books ever mention this alternate magic system from DA Mage. So, I would make the argument that these mechanical systems are no longer cannon. </div> </div> </div>You need to actually make an argument then, not just ignore what the world &quot;canon&quot; actually means. What is the argument to remove DA Mage's information about the setting, not just the systems for representing the setting, made with the Foundation/Pillars approach should no longer be canon? If it's just, &quot;M20 doesn't talk about it,&quot; that's on it's face just part of the assertion, not an argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, say one were to write a SV source-book or adventure set in the DA Mage era. </div> </div> </div>SV material is non-canon... so authors using Spheres in DA era games there doesn't change anything to the discussion at hand. Just like if Dataweaver decided to publish the Foundation/Pillars for Crafts and Disparates in the modern era as a book on SV wouldn't really matter to this conversation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not feel it is cool to require someone to track down and buy an old book that is otherwise imcompatible with the 600 page book that the adventure/sourcebook is based on. </div> </div> </div>Nobody's asking you to. You're being asked to consider that the canon setting of Mage as it stands includes that the Sphere system was not always how magic worked, because there's a canon book that contradicts that premise.<br /> <br /> That said, unless you're only going to look for copies from the original print run(s) of such books, most of them are very easy to &quot;track down.&quot; Just look for them on DriveThruRPG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384936-10-conventions-instead-of-5?p=1386181#post1386181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I *do* have is the entire M20 line, which should be more than enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enough to run and enjoy the game? Absolutely.<br /> <br /> Enough to get into a deep dive on any obscure lore point in the game... well maybe not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T14:33:42-07:00","id":1392049,"title":"","content":"So, revisiting this: <br /> <br /> Backing away from the \u201cOne Convention per Sphere\u201d idea and just tackling it as a general re-org of the Union, what would you do? Options include merging Conventions, splitting Conventions, a mix of the two, and/or rebranding existing Conventions. <br /> <br /> I would definitely go for splitting Panopticon off from its current masters and expanding it to a full-fledged espionage-oriented Convention, while the New World Order refocuses on politics and academics. <br /> <br /> Iteration X could probably do with a rebranding, since their name was a direct reference to the Computer (note the capitalization) and after the Dimensional Anomaly, that's no longer their thing. But I'm not sure what they should call themselves now. <br /> <br /> The Void Engineers could probably use a more militaristic name to go with their more militant attitude; but again, I'm not sure what would be a good name for them. <br /> <br /> The Syndicate probably doesn't need any rebranding, though I'm rather find of the suggestion from earlier in the thread that they call themselves the Invisible Hand. <br /> <br /> The Progenitors seem fine as is, as far as I'm concerned; but TR <i>did</i> make a suggestion not unlike reorganizing Iteration X and the Progenitors into three \u201cphysical sciences\u201d Conventions, one for physics (Iteration X), one for life sciences (the Progenitors), and one for chemistry. If we actually go with that, what would the chemistry-based one look like, and what might it be called?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T16:23:37-07:00","id":1394868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384936-10-conventions-instead-of-5?p=1392049#post1392049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iteration X could probably do with a rebranding, since their name was a direct reference to the Computer (note the capitalization) and after the Dimensional Anomaly, that's no longer their thing. But I'm not sure what they should call themselves now.</div> </div> </div> </div>ItX Revised said that they retained the name, rebranding it more to be about &quot;the next iteration of technology&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Void Engineers could probably use a more militaristic name to go with their more militant attitude; but again, I'm not sure what would be a good name for them. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Void Sentinels&quot; seems a fitting take.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T18:08:50-07:00","id":1394920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384936-10-conventions-instead-of-5?p=1394868#post1394868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ItX Revised said that they retained the name, rebranding it more to be about &quot;the next iteration of technology&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Though I'm curious: if you <i>had</i> to rename it, what would you call it? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384936-10-conventions-instead-of-5?p=1394868#post1394868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Void Sentinels&quot; seems a fitting take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, the Kickstarter draft of TR suggests that the Threat Null counterpart to the Void Engineers are the Sentinels. Though that's something that I disagree with, as I <i>don't</i> see the Threat Null counterpart being indistinguishable from the post-Anomaly version of the Convention. Rather, I see them as being a culmination of the <i>pre-</i>Anomaly Convention: VEs that finally abandoned Earth (willingly or not), fled into the Deep Universe driven by an urge to explore it (insert Star Trek reference here), and ended up \u201cgoing native\u201d. I'd either call them \u201cAliens\u201d or \u201cExplorers\u201d; but I wouldn't call them \u201cSentinels\u201d. <br /> <br /> With that long-winded explanation out of the way, I agree that something like \u201cSentinels of the Void\u201d or \u201cVoid Sentinels\u201d does indeed work for the post-Anomaly version of the Convention. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-13-2020, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T19:03:38-07:00","id":1394929,"title":"","content":"Void Sentinels sounds hella bad ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:04:58-07:00","id":1394949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384936-10-conventions-instead-of-5?p=1394929#post1394929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Void Sentinels sounds hella bad ass.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, it sounds awesome and scary as hell...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T16:12:41-07:00","id":1396515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384936-10-conventions-instead-of-5?p=1394920#post1394920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. Though I'm curious: if you <i>had</i> to rename it, what would you call it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, ItX has a very diverse bunch of themes - the robotics/AI science parts, the predictive/statistics elements, the mass-production/industrialisation stuff, the engineering/physics stuff and finally the military parts. Personally I would split it into two - a &quot;computer/robots/statistics convention&quot; which primarily made use of Data, Mind and Entropy with some Matter and Life and an &quot;engineering/physics convention&quot; which took the mass-production, military and engineering/physics themes and made use of Matter, Forces and Prime.<br /> <br /> The &quot;computer/robots/statistics&quot; convention would keep the name &quot;Iteration X&quot; while the other one would be the &quot;Macro-Engineers&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Progenitors seem fine as is, as far as I'm concerned; but TR <i>did</i> make a suggestion not unlike reorganizing Iteration X and the Progenitors into three \u201cphysical sciences\u201d Conventions, one for physics (Iteration X), one for life sciences (the Progenitors), and one for chemistry. If we actually go with that, what would the chemistry-based one look like, and what might it be called? </div> </div> </div>Obviously a primarily Matter-based Convention - would take up the Progenitors' shady links with the drug trade. I can see them playing around a lot with poisons and drugs of various kinds; also explosives. We can also tie this into material sciences in general - so stuff like memory metal, carbon nanotubes, various exotic elements etc. Still can't think of a name.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}